“ML Observatory: An AI-Driven Drift Detection & Auto-Remediation Platform”

🧠 What It Does:
Continuously monitors Azure ML-deployed models for data drift, model decay, and pipeline failures, and uses LLM agents to suggest or auto-fix the issue — via GitLab CI/CD.



🧠 Overview:
This architecture shows how a multi-agent AI system monitors ML models deployed in Azure, detects issues like data drift or performance drop, and automatically suggests or pushes fixes through GitLab CI/CD — all orchestrated using LangGraph.

🔷 Top-Level Flow (Left to Right)
1. 🖥️ React UI
Frontend dashboard for developers.

Shows live alerts: drift, performance drop, CI failures.

Users can view agent actions, suggestions, and fix PRs.

2. 🛠️ Node.js API
Backend API layer.

Handles requests from the UI, sends payloads to the orchestrator.

Retrieves logs, metrics, and current model metadata.

3. 🧠 LangGraph Orchestrator
Central brain of the system (agent router).

Receives input from API.

Uses MCP (Model Context Protocol) to understand context.

Routes tasks via AAP (Agent-to-Agent Protocol) to appropriate agents.

🤖 Agent Flow (Bottom Section)
4. 🧪 DriftDetectorAgent
Analyzes model input/output data.

Uses Azure Blob logs or built-in telemetry to detect feature drift or concept drift.

Sends result back to orchestrator.

5. 📊 PerformanceAgent
Pulls metrics from Azure ML (accuracy, latency, etc.).

Detects performance drops, stale models, etc.

Passes status to GitFixerAgent.

6. 🛠️ GitFixerAgent
LLM-powered agent that:

Analyzes issue

Auto-generates a fix (code snippet or CI config change)

Opens a GitLab Merge Request (MR) with proposed fixes

Uses GitLab API to push changes

7. 📬 NotifierAgent
Sends out notifications (Slack, Teams, Email) when:

Drift is detected

A fix is suggested or deployed

Retraining is triggered

☁️ Cloud + DevOps Flow (Top Right)
🔄 GitLab Repo
Central Git repository where code and CI/CD lives

GitFixerAgent submits MR (merge request) here

GitLab Pipelines handle retraining + redeployment

🔷 Azure ML
ML model is deployed here (real-time scoring endpoint)

Logs, metrics, and retraining run in Azure ML

GitLab pipeline connects to Azure ML SDK for deployments

🔁 Feedback Loop:
A model deployed in Azure shows issues (drift, perf drop).

Orchestrator routes to detection agents.

If fixable, GitFixerAgent proposes & pushes code changes to GitLab.

GitLab CI triggers retraining/redeployment in Azure ML.

UI shows results and Notifier alerts team.

✅ Outcome:
Self-healing ML models in production, with zero manual review required in early stages — and fully observable from your React dashboard.
